Third-party software this plugin interacts with (none of it is bundled or imported):

* pyserial (BSD-3-Clause) — declared Python dependency, used for port listing and serial capture.
  https://github.com/pyserial/pyserial

* esptool (GPL-2.0-or-later) — NOT a dependency and NOT imported. When the user calls
  esp32_chip_info, the plugin runs an esptool the user already has (a standalone esptool.exe
  installed by the Arduino ESP32 core / PlatformIO, or "<python> -m esptool") with only
  "--port <port> flash-id" (or chip-id) as a separate process and parses its text output.
  https://github.com/espressif/esptool

* Espressif GNU toolchain addr2line (GPL-3.0-or-later, binutils) — NOT bundled. Located on the
  user's machine (Arduino-ESP32 core, PlatformIO or ESP-IDF install) and run as a subprocess.

* esp-idf-monitor and esp-idf-panic-decoder (Apache-2.0, Espressif Systems) — no code was
  copied. The panic text formats recognised here (Guru Meditation header, register dump,
  "Backtrace: 0xPC:0xSP", "ELF file SHA256:", RISC-V MEPC/RA) and the idea of resolving them
  with "addr2line -pfiaC -e <elf>" follow the behaviour of these Apache-2.0 projects, which is
  acknowledged here. https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf-monitor
  https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf-panic-decoder
